CM_ "Virtual-bus view of the ARS510 0x80 / 0x85 records. Only valid for logs produced by tools/build_cabana_route.py.";
CM_ BO_ 1792 "Reassembled 0x80 object slot 0 (record bytes 17-52), sent only when occupied. Little-endian bit field: bit 0 = LSB of slot byte 0.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 STATE_CODE "Track state: 1 update-like, 2 prediction-like/coasting candidate; 0 rare. While 2, SCORE_CODE drops by 20 (or 1) per cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 SLOT_INDEX_CODE "Physical slot index 0-19; 63 when the slot is unallocated.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_8_6 "Bits 8-12: startup code, min(30, floor(31 * (2/3)^max(age - 4, 0))) while the motion code is 5 (initializing). Bit 13: separate raw flag.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 ONCOMING_FLAG "Oncoming-like internal motion state. Can persist after slowing and reset before the native allocation ends.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_15_1 "Raw; mostly set on newborn zero-range rows.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 SCORE_CODE "Existence probability, percent (10-100): can decline in either state; drops by exactly 20 (or 1) per cycle in state 2 and may stay lowered after a return to state 1. Bits 20-22 are its bits 4-6 (score // 16). The slot is freed near 20.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 AGE "Track age in radar cycles (60 ms): 1 at birth, saturates at 126; 0 = slot retiring. A restart is a new track. Converged from about 60.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_31_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 DREL "Distance forward of the radar, m: (code - 160) / 16. Add 1.52 m for openpilot's camera-referenced distance (radard does).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 YREL_LEFT "Lateral offset, m, left positive: (code - 2048) * 0.015. |code - 2048| >= 2000 is a sentinel.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_56_7 "Object length, about 0.1 m per code: car ~4.9 m, large vehicle ~5.7 m, two-wheeler ~1.7 m, pedestrian ~0.4 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_63_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 VLONG_OVER_GROUND "Longitudinal velocity over ground, m/s: (code - 510.5) * 0.15. vRel = this - ego speed. Code 1023 is a saturated reading.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 VLAT_OVER_GROUND_PROV "Lateral velocity over ground, m/s, left positive: (code - 510.5) * about 0.142-0.147 (0.15 used).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 ALONG_LIKE_84 "Longitudinal acceleration over ground, filtered: (code - 511) * about 0.04 m/s^2; follows velocity by 0.5-1 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_94_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_96 "Lateral acceleration over ground, filtered: (code - 511) * 0.05 m/s^2; follows the kinematic value by about 0.5 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_106_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_107_1 "Predicted (not measured) record, like Tesla's Meas = 0: set on 45 % of a track's last five records, 2.6 % elsewhere.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_108_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 MOVE_STATE "Low two bits of the motion code. Full code = MOVE_STATE | (UNK_111_1 << 2): 0 moving forward, 1 slow or standing, 2 oncoming, 3 moving right, 4 moving left, 5 initializing, 7 stopped after moving.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_111_1 "Bit 2 of the motion code (see MOVE_STATE).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_112_3 "Camera-association state: 0 radar only, 1 (rarely 2-4) while the camera has the vehicle. By day non-zero on nearly all in-lane vehicles inside 40 m and almost never beyond 50 m; at night also at long range.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_115_5 "Class confidence in 5 % steps: 0 while not yet classified, 4-20 otherwise (20 = 100 %); moves by one step per cycle. A large vehicle is re-classified as a car when it falls to 5.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_120_3 "Raw; non-zero on 0.2 % of rows (mature cars).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_123_5 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_128_2 "Lane-assignment state, low bits (full = UNK_128_2 | UNK_130_1 << 2): 3 ego lane, 2 right lane, 4 left lane; 1, 5, 7 = no lane weights.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_130_1 "Lane-assignment state, bit 2 (see UNK_128_2).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_131_4 "Dominant lane weight: the largest of the three lane weights or one less.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_135_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_136_4 "Camera-association confidence: 15 without association; restarts at 3-9 when UNK_112_3 becomes non-zero and climbs to 14.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_140_3 "Object class, second encoding of UNK_163_3: 0, 5, 7, 1, 3, 4 = class 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_143_5 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_148_8 "Lane weights in 1/15 steps: low nibble (148|4) right lane, high nibble (152|4) left lane. With UNK_156_4 (ego lane) they sum to 15 or 16.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_156_4 "Ego-lane weight in 1/15 steps (see UNK_148_8).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_160_3 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_163_3 "Object class: 1 not yet classified, 2 car, 3 large vehicle, 4 pedestrian, 5 provisional (cyclist / person associations), 6 two-wheeler.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_166_2 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_168_10 "All ones or all zeros (768 / 832 rare): a per-track pattern of k cycles on in every 5, locked to the track's age; k follows the range where the track was first seen (far: always on).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_178_3 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_181_1 "Daylight flag: set on a quarter of mature vehicle rows by day (cars and large vehicles, more often far out) and on 2 of 59,988 night rows.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_182_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_183_7 "Bit 183 raw; bits 184-189 are the low bits of a secondary score byte 184|8 (percent: 100 on 98 % of rows, 60-99 on young tracks).";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_190_10 "Bits 190-191 = top of the secondary score byte 184|8; bits 192-199 are zero.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_200_7 "Orientation uncertainty: about 3.1 * UNK_248_7 / speed (m/s) on moving objects; 63 for stopped objects, 127 sentinel. Keep all seven bits.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_207_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_208_6 "Coarse heading over ground, left positive, about pi/64 rad per code: matches floor(max(atan2(vy, vx), 0) * 64 / pi) on 98 % of settled moving samples; can update while both velocity codes hold.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_214_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_216_6 "Object width, about (code + 1) * 0.1 m: car ~1.8 m, large vehicle ~2.0 m, two-wheeler ~0.7 m, pedestrian ~0.5 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_222_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_224_7 "Range standard deviation (sigma dRel), about 0.23 m per count below 40 m: grows with range, shrinks with track age.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_231_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_232_7 "Lateral standard deviation (sigma yRel), about 0.10 m per count: grows with |yRel|, shrinks with age.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_239_1 "Raw; often set near track birth.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_240_7 "Longitudinal velocity standard deviation (sigma vx), about 0.043-0.045 m/s per count against the ACC target: grows with range, higher during velocity excursions. 127 accompanies saturated velocity.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_247_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_248_7 "Lateral velocity standard deviation (sigma vy), about 0.37 m/s per count.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 CONST_255_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_256_6 "Longitudinal-acceleration standard deviation (candidate sigma ax), low bits of 256|8: grows with range and with track age.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_262_2 "Upper bits of the candidate sigma ax at 256.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_264_5 "Lateral-acceleration standard deviation (candidate sigma ay), low bits of 264|8: about 11 at age 5-10, 2 from age 40.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_269_3 "Upper bits of the candidate sigma ay at 264.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_272_5 "Height-like size code (candidate); larger for large vehicles.";
CM_ SG_ 1792 UNK_277_11 "Raw; bit 277 rarely set on newborn tracks.";
CM_ BO_ 1793 "Reassembled 0x80 object slot 1 (record bytes 53-88), sent only when occupied. Little-endian bit field: bit 0 = LSB of slot byte 0.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 STATE_CODE "Track state: 1 update-like, 2 prediction-like/coasting candidate; 0 rare. While 2, SCORE_CODE drops by 20 (or 1) per cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 SLOT_INDEX_CODE "Physical slot index 0-19; 63 when the slot is unallocated.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_8_6 "Bits 8-12: startup code, min(30, floor(31 * (2/3)^max(age - 4, 0))) while the motion code is 5 (initializing). Bit 13: separate raw flag.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 ONCOMING_FLAG "Oncoming-like internal motion state. Can persist after slowing and reset before the native allocation ends.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_15_1 "Raw; mostly set on newborn zero-range rows.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 SCORE_CODE "Existence probability, percent (10-100): can decline in either state; drops by exactly 20 (or 1) per cycle in state 2 and may stay lowered after a return to state 1. Bits 20-22 are its bits 4-6 (score // 16). The slot is freed near 20.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 AGE "Track age in radar cycles (60 ms): 1 at birth, saturates at 126; 0 = slot retiring. A restart is a new track. Converged from about 60.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 CONST_31_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 DREL "Distance forward of the radar, m: (code - 160) / 16. Add 1.52 m for openpilot's camera-referenced distance (radard does).";
CM_ SG_ 1793 YREL_LEFT "Lateral offset, m, left positive: (code - 2048) * 0.015. |code - 2048| >= 2000 is a sentinel.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_56_7 "Object length, about 0.1 m per code: car ~4.9 m, large vehicle ~5.7 m, two-wheeler ~1.7 m, pedestrian ~0.4 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_63_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 VLONG_OVER_GROUND "Longitudinal velocity over ground, m/s: (code - 510.5) * 0.15. vRel = this - ego speed. Code 1023 is a saturated reading.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 VLAT_OVER_GROUND_PROV "Lateral velocity over ground, m/s, left positive: (code - 510.5) * about 0.142-0.147 (0.15 used).";
CM_ SG_ 1793 ALONG_LIKE_84 "Longitudinal acceleration over ground, filtered: (code - 511) * about 0.04 m/s^2; follows velocity by 0.5-1 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 CONST_94_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_96 "Lateral acceleration over ground, filtered: (code - 511) * 0.05 m/s^2; follows the kinematic value by about 0.5 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_106_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_107_1 "Predicted (not measured) record, like Tesla's Meas = 0: set on 45 % of a track's last five records, 2.6 % elsewhere.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 CONST_108_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 MOVE_STATE "Low two bits of the motion code. Full code = MOVE_STATE | (UNK_111_1 << 2): 0 moving forward, 1 slow or standing, 2 oncoming, 3 moving right, 4 moving left, 5 initializing, 7 stopped after moving.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_111_1 "Bit 2 of the motion code (see MOVE_STATE).";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_112_3 "Camera-association state: 0 radar only, 1 (rarely 2-4) while the camera has the vehicle. By day non-zero on nearly all in-lane vehicles inside 40 m and almost never beyond 50 m; at night also at long range.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_115_5 "Class confidence in 5 % steps: 0 while not yet classified, 4-20 otherwise (20 = 100 %); moves by one step per cycle. A large vehicle is re-classified as a car when it falls to 5.";
CM_ SG_ 1793 UNK_120_3 "Raw; non-zero on 0.2 % of rows (mature cars).";
