CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_208_6 "Coarse heading over ground, left positive, about pi/64 rad per code: matches floor(max(atan2(vy, vx), 0) * 64 / pi) on 98 % of settled moving samples; can update while both velocity codes hold.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 CONST_214_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_216_6 "Object width, about (code + 1) * 0.1 m: car ~1.8 m, large vehicle ~2.0 m, two-wheeler ~0.7 m, pedestrian ~0.5 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 CONST_222_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_224_7 "Range standard deviation (sigma dRel), about 0.23 m per count below 40 m: grows with range, shrinks with track age.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 CONST_231_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_232_7 "Lateral standard deviation (sigma yRel), about 0.10 m per count: grows with |yRel|, shrinks with age.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_239_1 "Raw; often set near track birth.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_240_7 "Longitudinal velocity standard deviation (sigma vx), about 0.043-0.045 m/s per count against the ACC target: grows with range, higher during velocity excursions. 127 accompanies saturated velocity.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 CONST_247_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_248_7 "Lateral velocity standard deviation (sigma vy), about 0.37 m/s per count.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 CONST_255_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_256_6 "Longitudinal-acceleration standard deviation (candidate sigma ax), low bits of 256|8: grows with range and with track age.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_262_2 "Upper bits of the candidate sigma ax at 256.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_264_5 "Lateral-acceleration standard deviation (candidate sigma ay), low bits of 264|8: about 11 at age 5-10, 2 from age 40.";
