CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_272_5 "Height-like size code (candidate); larger for large vehicles.";
CM_ SG_ 1795 UNK_277_11 "Raw; bit 277 rarely set on newborn tracks.";
CM_ BO_ 1796 "Reassembled 0x80 object slot 4 (record bytes 161-196), sent only when occupied. Little-endian bit field: bit 0 = LSB of slot byte 0.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 STATE_CODE "Track state: 1 update-like, 2 prediction-like/coasting candidate; 0 rare. While 2, SCORE_CODE drops by 20 (or 1) per cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 SLOT_INDEX_CODE "Physical slot index 0-19; 63 when the slot is unallocated.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_8_6 "Bits 8-12: startup code, min(30, floor(31 * (2/3)^max(age - 4, 0))) while the motion code is 5 (initializing). Bit 13: separate raw flag.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 ONCOMING_FLAG "Oncoming-like internal motion state. Can persist after slowing and reset before the native allocation ends.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_15_1 "Raw; mostly set on newborn zero-range rows.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 SCORE_CODE "Existence probability, percent (10-100): can decline in either state; drops by exactly 20 (or 1) per cycle in state 2 and may stay lowered after a return to state 1. Bits 20-22 are its bits 4-6 (score // 16). The slot is freed near 20.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 AGE "Track age in radar cycles (60 ms): 1 at birth, saturates at 126; 0 = slot retiring. A restart is a new track. Converged from about 60.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_31_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 DREL "Distance forward of the radar, m: (code - 160) / 16. Add 1.52 m for openpilot's camera-referenced distance (radard does).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 YREL_LEFT "Lateral offset, m, left positive: (code - 2048) * 0.015. |code - 2048| >= 2000 is a sentinel.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_56_7 "Object length, about 0.1 m per code: car ~4.9 m, large vehicle ~5.7 m, two-wheeler ~1.7 m, pedestrian ~0.4 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_63_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 VLONG_OVER_GROUND "Longitudinal velocity over ground, m/s: (code - 510.5) * 0.15. vRel = this - ego speed. Code 1023 is a saturated reading.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 VLAT_OVER_GROUND_PROV "Lateral velocity over ground, m/s, left positive: (code - 510.5) * about 0.142-0.147 (0.15 used).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 ALONG_LIKE_84 "Longitudinal acceleration over ground, filtered: (code - 511) * about 0.04 m/s^2; follows velocity by 0.5-1 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_94_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_96 "Lateral acceleration over ground, filtered: (code - 511) * 0.05 m/s^2; follows the kinematic value by about 0.5 s.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_106_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_107_1 "Predicted (not measured) record, like Tesla's Meas = 0: set on 45 % of a track's last five records, 2.6 % elsewhere.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_108_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 MOVE_STATE "Low two bits of the motion code. Full code = MOVE_STATE | (UNK_111_1 << 2): 0 moving forward, 1 slow or standing, 2 oncoming, 3 moving right, 4 moving left, 5 initializing, 7 stopped after moving.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_111_1 "Bit 2 of the motion code (see MOVE_STATE).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_112_3 "Camera-association state: 0 radar only, 1 (rarely 2-4) while the camera has the vehicle. By day non-zero on nearly all in-lane vehicles inside 40 m and almost never beyond 50 m; at night also at long range.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_115_5 "Class confidence in 5 % steps: 0 while not yet classified, 4-20 otherwise (20 = 100 %); moves by one step per cycle. A large vehicle is re-classified as a car when it falls to 5.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_120_3 "Raw; non-zero on 0.2 % of rows (mature cars).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_123_5 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_128_2 "Lane-assignment state, low bits (full = UNK_128_2 | UNK_130_1 << 2): 3 ego lane, 2 right lane, 4 left lane; 1, 5, 7 = no lane weights.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_130_1 "Lane-assignment state, bit 2 (see UNK_128_2).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_131_4 "Dominant lane weight: the largest of the three lane weights or one less.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_135_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_136_4 "Camera-association confidence: 15 without association; restarts at 3-9 when UNK_112_3 becomes non-zero and climbs to 14.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_140_3 "Object class, second encoding of UNK_163_3: 0, 5, 7, 1, 3, 4 = class 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_143_5 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_148_8 "Lane weights in 1/15 steps: low nibble (148|4) right lane, high nibble (152|4) left lane. With UNK_156_4 (ego lane) they sum to 15 or 16.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_156_4 "Ego-lane weight in 1/15 steps (see UNK_148_8).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_160_3 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_163_3 "Object class: 1 not yet classified, 2 car, 3 large vehicle, 4 pedestrian, 5 provisional (cyclist / person associations), 6 two-wheeler.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_166_2 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_168_10 "All ones or all zeros (768 / 832 rare): a per-track pattern of k cycles on in every 5, locked to the track's age; k follows the range where the track was first seen (far: always on).";
CM_ SG_ 1796 CONST_178_3 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1796 UNK_181_1 "Daylight flag: set on a quarter of mature vehicle rows by day (cars and large vehicles, more often far out) and on 2 of 59,988 night rows.";
