CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_131_4 "Dominant lane weight: the largest of the three lane weights or one less.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_135_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_136_4 "Camera-association confidence: 15 without association; restarts at 3-9 when UNK_112_3 becomes non-zero and climbs to 14.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_140_3 "Object class, second encoding of UNK_163_3: 0, 5, 7, 1, 3, 4 = class 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_143_5 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_148_8 "Lane weights in 1/15 steps: low nibble (148|4) right lane, high nibble (152|4) left lane. With UNK_156_4 (ego lane) they sum to 15 or 16.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_156_4 "Ego-lane weight in 1/15 steps (see UNK_148_8).";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_160_3 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_163_3 "Object class: 1 not yet classified, 2 car, 3 large vehicle, 4 pedestrian, 5 provisional (cyclist / person associations), 6 two-wheeler.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_166_2 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_168_10 "All ones or all zeros (768 / 832 rare): a per-track pattern of k cycles on in every 5, locked to the track's age; k follows the range where the track was first seen (far: always on).";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_178_3 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_181_1 "Daylight flag: set on a quarter of mature vehicle rows by day (cars and large vehicles, more often far out) and on 2 of 59,988 night rows.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_182_1 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_183_7 "Bit 183 raw; bits 184-189 are the low bits of a secondary score byte 184|8 (percent: 100 on 98 % of rows, 60-99 on young tracks).";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_190_10 "Bits 190-191 = top of the secondary score byte 184|8; bits 192-199 are zero.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_200_7 "Orientation uncertainty: about 3.1 * UNK_248_7 / speed (m/s) on moving objects; 63 for stopped objects, 127 sentinel. Keep all seven bits.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_207_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_208_6 "Coarse heading over ground, left positive, about pi/64 rad per code: matches floor(max(atan2(vy, vx), 0) * 64 / pi) on 98 % of settled moving samples; can update while both velocity codes hold.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_214_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_216_6 "Object width, about (code + 1) * 0.1 m: car ~1.8 m, large vehicle ~2.0 m, two-wheeler ~0.7 m, pedestrian ~0.5 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_222_2 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_224_7 "Range standard deviation (sigma dRel), about 0.23 m per count below 40 m: grows with range, shrinks with track age.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_231_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_232_7 "Lateral standard deviation (sigma yRel), about 0.10 m per count: grows with |yRel|, shrinks with age.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_239_1 "Raw; often set near track birth.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_240_7 "Longitudinal velocity standard deviation (sigma vx), about 0.043-0.045 m/s per count against the ACC target: grows with range, higher during velocity excursions. 127 accompanies saturated velocity.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_247_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_248_7 "Lateral velocity standard deviation (sigma vy), about 0.37 m/s per count.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 CONST_255_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_256_6 "Longitudinal-acceleration standard deviation (candidate sigma ax), low bits of 256|8: grows with range and with track age.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_262_2 "Upper bits of the candidate sigma ax at 256.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_264_5 "Lateral-acceleration standard deviation (candidate sigma ay), low bits of 264|8: about 11 at age 5-10, 2 from age 40.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_269_3 "Upper bits of the candidate sigma ay at 264.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_272_5 "Height-like size code (candidate); larger for large vehicles.";
CM_ SG_ 1811 UNK_277_11 "Raw; bit 277 rarely set on newborn tracks.";
CM_ BO_ 1824 "NOT radar bytes: values the ars510 interface computes for 0x80 slot 0, for plotting next to the raw fields.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 TRACK_ID_OP "trackId openpilot would see under the raw profile, BASE_CONFIG (held until age 60, re-link within 3.5 s); 0 when not published.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 TRACK_ID_RAW "trackId from the radar slot/age lifecycle alone (ALL_TRACKS_CONFIG).";
CM_ SG_ 1824 VREL "VLONG_OVER_GROUND - Toyota 0xB4 speed, m/s.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 V_EGO_0xB4 "Toyota 0xB4 SPEED used for VREL, m/s (reads ~1-1.5% below GPS / wheel speed).";
CM_ SG_ 1824 DREL_FUSED "Velocity-aided range (range_fusion_gain 0.1, part of the fused profile); cuts short-term range walks by about a third.";
CM_ SG_ 1824 VREL_KALMAN "vRel from the fused profile's Kalman speed filter (object list and ACC target weighted by their uncertainty), on every track from age 1 and at the nominal 0.15 m/s per code.";
