CM_ BO_ 1856 "0x80 record bytes 0-16, before the 20 object slots. Byte 0 is 0xE4 (transport length low byte).";
CM_ SG_ 1856 CONST_HDR0_8 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR8_5 "Part of the clock code in record bytes 1-4 (little-endian), which equals the 0x85 fine clock // 100.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR13_4 "Part of the clock code in record bytes 1-4 (see UNK_HDR8_5).";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR17_15 "Part of the clock code in record bytes 1-4 (see UNK_HDR8_5).";
CM_ SG_ 1856 CONST_HDR32_1 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR33_1 "Part of the clock code in record bytes 1-4 (see UNK_HDR8_5).";
CM_ SG_ 1856 CONST_HDR34_7 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR41_15 "Record counter: record bytes 5-6 (little-endian) >> 1; equals the 0x85 counter of the same cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 CONST_HDR56_12 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR68_4 "Raw, unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 CONST_HDR72_32 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR104_3 "Timing-offset candidate (104|11 region): its change tracks the record's arrival-time offset at about 1 ms per count.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR107_4 "Timing-offset candidate (see UNK_HDR104_3).";
CM_ SG_ 1856 UNK_HDR111_4 "Raw; usually 3.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 OBJECT_COUNT "Number of allocated slots: those whose index field equals their position, which are the slots with age >= 1. Allocated slots need not be the first N.";
CM_ SG_ 1856 CONST_HDR120_16 "Constant in the captured data.";
CM_ SG_ 1857 RECORD_CRC32 "zlib CRC32 over record bytes 1-736, little-endian; failing records are not exported.";
CM_ BO_ 1888 "0x85 record bytes 0-20 (prefix). Byte 0 is the length-low byte 0x90; bytes 1-4 fine clock, 5-6 counter.";
CM_ SG_ 1889 PARAMETERS_PRESENT "1 = the cell holds parameters (bytes 6-9 differ from the default 84 03 F4 01).";
CM_ SG_ 1889 CURVE_OFFSET_M "c0: (32|12 - 2000) * 0.01 m, left positive. Meaningful when PARAMETERS_PRESENT = 1.";
